---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import GamePlayer from '../../components/GamePlayer.astro';
import AdSlot from '../../components/AdSlot.astro';
import games from '../../data/games.json';
import skills from '../../data/skills.json';
import { url } from '../../config';

const game = games.find(g => g.id === 'addition-grade-1')!;
const skill = skills[game.skill as keyof typeof skills];
const page = new URL(url('math-games/addition-for-grade-1/'), Astro.site).href;
const jsonLd = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'LearningResource', name: `${game.keywordTitle}: ${game.title}`,
    url: page, description: game.summary, isAccessibleForFree: true, inLanguage: 'en',
    learningResourceType: 'Educational game', educationalLevel: 'Grade 1', typicalAgeRange: '6-7',
    teaches: 'Addition within 20', timeRequired: 'PT3M', image: new URL(url(game.poster), Astro.site).href,
  },
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'BreadcrumbList', itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: new URL(url(), Astro.site).href },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Math games', item: new URL(url('math-games/'), Astro.site).href },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 3, name: game.keywordTitle, item: page },
    ],
  },
];
---
<Base
  title="Addition for Grade 1: Free Math Game for Ages 6 to 7 | EduLearnLabs"
  description="A free addition game for Grade 1. Kids fill a basket for a garden customer, add within 20 and grow their own garden. Friendly hints, no ads, no login, 3 minutes a game."
  path="math-games/addition-for-grade-1/" nav="math" image={game.poster} jsonLd={jsonLd}>

  <Breadcrumbs back={{ name: 'Math games', path: 'math-games/' }}
    items={[{ name: 'Home', path: '' }, { name: 'Math games', path: 'math-games/' }, { name: game.keywordTitle, path: 'math-games/addition-for-grade-1/' }]} />

  <h1>Addition for Grade 1</h1>
  <p class="lead" style="font-size:20px;max-width:44em">Play <strong>{game.title}</strong>: help garden friends fill
    their baskets, add numbers up to 20 and grow your own garden. Ten orders, about 3 minutes, free.</p>

  <GamePlayer game={game} topDifficulty={skill.topDifficulty} />

  <section class="prose">
    <h2>What is Addition Garden?</h2>
    <p>Addition Garden is a short math game for first graders, played at a little flower stall run by Hazel the owl.
      A ladybug, snail, bee or rabbit comes by and asks for flowers, like "3 sunflowers and 4 daisies, please".
      Your child drags the flowers from two bins into a basket, and the bunch comes together. Then comes the real
      question: how many in all? Your child taps one of three answers. After ten orders the game ends with stars,
      and every order your child solved plants a seed in their own garden.</p>

    <h2>What kids learn</h2>
    <p>The game practices adding within 20, a core Grade 1 skill. Children do not just pick an answer. They put two
      groups together with their hands and see the total appear, which is exactly what addition means. It moves
      through five small steps:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Sums up to 5, like 2 + 3</li>
      <li>Sums up to 10, like 6 + 4</li>
      <li>Bigger sums up to 10, like 8 + 2</li>
      <li>Teen numbers plus a small number, like 12 + 5, on two ten-frames of stepping stones in a pond</li>
      <li>Sums that cross ten, like 8 + 7, by filling up the first ten-frame and then adding the rest</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Who it is for</h2>
    <p>Children in Grade 1, usually ages 6 and 7. It also suits Kindergarten children who already count well and
      Grade 2 children who want quick, confident practice. Every order is spoken aloud, so early readers can play
      alone. It works best on a tablet, a computer or a phone held sideways.</p>

    <h2>How to play</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Press Play, then tap the big button to start.</li>
      <li>Listen to the order, then drag flowers from the bins into the basket. You can also tap a bin and then tap
        the basket.</li>
      <li>When the basket is full, tap how many flowers there are in all.</li>
      <li>Not sure? Hazel helps. She points at the order, counts along with you, and never gives the answer away.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>Your own garden</h2>
    <p>Each solved order plants a seed. As your child plays more games, the seeds sprout and bloom into sunflowers,
      tulips, daisies, lavender, strawberry plants and little trees. Plants only grow when your child plays, so
      there is no pressure and nothing ever wilts. The garden is saved on your own device, and the game never asks
      for a name, an email or a login.</p>

    <h2>Why it helps</h2>
    <p>The game starts easy and steps up after three right answers in a row, then steps back after two misses, so
      your child practices at the right level. Mistakes are never a dead end: the flower simply hops back, a wrong
      choice fades, and your child makes the last tap. Orders your child missed come back in the next game for
      another go. And because the wrong choices are real mistakes, like being one away or subtracting instead of
      adding, the <a href={url('grown-ups/')}>Grown-ups page</a> can tell you what to practice together.</p>
    <p class="note">More to play: see all <a href={url('math-games/')}>free math games</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <AdSlot id="game-bottom" />
</Base>
